<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joscelin I, Count of Edessa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1131</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Joscelin of Courtenay</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joscelin I of Courtenay was count of Edessa from 1118 to 1131, after holding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turbessel">Turbessel</a> as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of his cousin Baldwin II. A tireless fighter against the Turks, he was captured at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a> in 1104 and again by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belek-ghazi">Belek Ghazi</a> in 1122, escaping the next year from the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harput">Harput</a>. He died in 1131 of wounds received during a siege.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joscelin-i-count-of-edessa.jpg" alt="Joscelin I, Count of Edessa" width="320" height="313" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joscelin_I_of_Edessa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
